       "text": "I didn't enter this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the labeled maximum of 200 mg per day for adults. That dose could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity.\n\nIs 1000 mg a typo? Here are two options:\n- **Usual dosing:** Start at 25\u201350 mg once daily and titrate. The maximum is 200 mg per day.\n- **Different dose:** If you meant another dose, tell me the dose and I'll enter it.\n\nI can't enter a dose above the labeled maximum, even if it has been approved elsewhere. If you need a higher dose for an unusual reason, please talk to pharmacy or the attending physician."
